{"uid":"modules/bsb_compat.py","name":"bsb_compat.py","qualname":"modules/bsb_compat.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/bsb_compat.py","line":1,"end_line":271,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"BlackSandBeacon wire-protocol compatibility helpers.","description":"BlackSandBeacon beacons derive their working AES key from the raw C2 key\nmaterial with HKDF-SHA256 (salt ``blacksandbeacon-v2``, info ``enc`` /\n``hmac``), so their traffic never uses the on-disk key directly. Every\nbeacon report also carries a replay-protection envelope: the plaintext is\n``counter (8 bytes LE) || timestamp (8 bytes LE) || payload``.\n\nThe C2 speaks the legacy protocol (raw key, no envelope) for its own\nbeacons, so these helpers derive the matching BSB keys from the same\non-disk key file and decode the envelope. Result handling tries the\nlegacy format first and falls back to BSB, so both client families check\nin against the same C2.\n\nContracts:\n    - ``derive_bsb_keys``: HKDF-SHA256 key separation matching BSB's C code.\n    - ``decrypt_bsb_report``: decode one BSB report (b64 IV + ciphertext).\n    - ``encrypt_bsb_command``: legacy wire format under the BSB-derived key.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/bsb_compat.py::HKDF_SALT","modules/bsb_compat.py::STAGE_HKDF_SALT","modules/bsb_compat.py::REPLAY_HEADER_BYTES","modules/bsb_compat.py::derive_bsb_keys","modules/bsb_compat.py::decrypt_bsb_report","modules/bsb_compat.py::encrypt_bsb_command","modules/bsb_compat.py::derive_bsb_stage_keys","modules/bsb_compat.py::encrypt_bsb_stage_blob","modules/bsb_compat.py::decrypt_bsb_stage_blob"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
